Description: avformat: write the frame packing SEI of an HEVC stream
 The consumer puts the stereo3d packing on each frame, where libx264 writes the
 H.264 frame packing arrangement SEI, and on the stream, where the muxers write
 Matroska's StereoMode and MP4's st3d. libx265 reads no Stereo 3D frame data, so
 an HEVC render carried the container's mark and no SEI (H.265 D.2.16, D.3.16),
 which a 3D television's own player and an SEI-only reader need.
 .
 When stereo3d is set and the encoder is HEVC and not one that writes the SEI
 itself (hevc_vaapi, hevc_nvenc, hevc_qsv, hevc_vulkan in the edition's FFmpeg),
 the packets go through FFmpeg's hevc_metadata bitstream filter with
 frame_packing=insert, which takes the layout from the stream's Stereo 3D side
 data and clears general_non_packed_constraint_flag in the parameter sets, as
 H.265 7.4.4 requires; its extradata replaces the stream's before the header is
 written, and the filter is drained at the end. An FFmpeg whose hevc_metadata
 lacks the option makes the consumer say so in its log; the container's mark is
 still written.
 .
 Measured: melt with vcodec=libx265 stereo3d=side_by_side, MP4 (strict=-1) and
 Matroska: before, 0 frame packing SEI; after, type 3, content interpretation 1,
 read back by FFmpeg's trace_headers. H.264 output unchanged.
